A||||25||JohnnyK||New clue for you guys to solve my hard shifting problems||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||08-30-2000||07:19 PM||||Well, it is becoming real difficult to shift into gears (just downshifting or stopped with the clutch in). However, I did notice that then shifting action is smooth when the car is not running. Does this rule out the fact that it could be a linkage adjustment (I did that, didn't seem to help). Also, if I push it up, trying to get into first (it takes all my strength sometimes), when I slow down and the speed approaches about 10mpg, it just glides into first. Any ideas? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||08-30-2000||08:54 PM||||Sounds like clutch bleeding time.||||reg||1
